  "transformation_steps": [
    "Read cropped_mesh.obj and convert its y-up axes to the COLMAP world frame: (x, y, z) -> (x, -z, y).",
    "Project every mesh vertex into every view with the COLMAP pose and pinhole intrinsics.",
    "Label a vertex as wound when, among views where it faces the camera, more than half of the masks are > 40/255 at its pixel; keep the largest connected wound patch.",
    "Build a tangent frame by PCA of the skin within 2.5 wound radii; align e1 with the wound's long axis.",
    "Resample the mesh as a 0.1 mDU height field by linear interpolation.",
    "Fit a quadratic surface to the healthy ring (band up to 0.4 wound radii outside the wound) and use it as the illustrative operator-accepted target.",
    "Tile the wound with the modules.honeycomb lattice and run the previous whole-cell staged fill (kept as the audited baseline V1_LATTICE).",
    "Classify every height-field pixel with the unchanged safety rules (pipeline.coverage.eligibility): edge margin, surface support, uncertainty gate and at least one layer of room below the lower envelope.",
    "Search hexagon side (5 sizes from the previous side down to two strand widths), rotation (0-50 deg in 10 deg steps) and 16 staggered offsets for three planners: whole cells, adaptive whole cells and whole cells plus boundary cells clipped to the eligible region (clipped piece >= 1/4 hexagon and >= 2 strand widths wide).",
    "Stage the fill one whole layer per accepted cell below the lower envelope; re-measure and repeat until no cell has room; count every boundary, support, envelope and self-intersection violation.",
    "Select the first planner (whole -> adaptive -> clipped) with zero violations and >= 90% eligible-area coverage; otherwise report the best coverage as PARTIAL.",
    "Map the scaffold and toolpath back to world coordinates and project them into the display photograph.",
    "Vertex colours for the 3D panels are sampled from the display photograph; no numbers are taken from RGB pixels."
  ],
